#{[17592186387569 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}-2{e}^{3-2t}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t)\\,dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387569 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387569 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b081a3f8-5d8f-5f9a-99c1-6db960fad9c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387570 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2+3t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2t)\\,dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387570 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387570 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6cb1ba5a-5c13-5cea-85f4-897235a023e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387571 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-2t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)\\,dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387571 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387571 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "24e2f8ba-dc02-5934-b9c4-730a95923e0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387572 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3-2t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+3t)\\,dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387572 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387572 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf295d2c-d5ca-5154-8827-1597a93d6e02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387573 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{e}^{2+3t}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2t)\\,dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387573 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387573 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d1d48b2e-8bb9-5e98-bb9f-2d4fb900164b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387616 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387616 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387616 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387616 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f7/f7bacafcbe893c0d21ea45a916190a49aa3a3532834cff4704f707c100bf8e6a.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=3y\\,i+2x\\,j$ and $C$ is the the arc of the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $1$ and $3$ respectively, traversed anticlockwise from $A(0,3)$ to $B(-1,0)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387616 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "650eb0a9-0597-5e63-9ed1-143928ee022a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387616 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find the parametrization of an ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $1$ and $3$ respectively. It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =3y\\,i+2x\\,j \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-9{sin}^{2}⁡t+6{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =6{cos}^{2}⁡t-9{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(6{cos}^{2}⁡t-9{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387617 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387617