078 #edb/ref 17592186414864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414911 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a60002fd-79c9-55af-8350-d15ad8aa640e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186414878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414912 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c6e03b21-80ec-5be8-9b81-321307ca2b39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414918 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414918 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414918 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414918 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of a circle of radius $3$ centered at the origin traversed counterclockwise from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(-3,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414918 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17a6c1da-e7e7-5509-a937-e43376741415" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414918 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a part-circle of radius $3$ centered at the origin. This curve can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+9{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+9{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+27{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(3{sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(3{sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(3{sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,dt \\\\  & =9{[{sin}^{3}⁡t-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{2}]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =9[0-(1-\\frac{1}{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414922 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414922 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125044" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414922 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414922 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(x+y)^{2}\\,i+{e}^{x-y}\\,j$ and $C$ is the line segment traversed from the point $A(-2,1)$ to the point $B(1,-1)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(-2+3t)\\,i+(1-2t)\\,j.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414922 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6205682e-6a34-5394-bdf6-22819f2b4d42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414922 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the line segment.\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are \n$a=-2\\,i+j$ and $b=i-j.$\nSo, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =(-2\\,i+j)+t[(i-j)-(-2\\,i+j)] \\\\  & =(-2\\,i+j)+t(3\\,i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =(-2+3t)\\,i+(1-2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ varies from $t=0$ (at the point $A$) to $t=1$ (at the point $B$).\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=-2+3t,\\,y=1-2t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x+y)^{2}\\,i+{e}^{x-y}\\,j \\\\  & =(-2+3t+1-2t)^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2+3t-(1-2t)}\\,j \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\,i+{e}^{5t-3}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2+3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i-2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((t-1)^{2}\\,i+{e}^{5t-2}\\,j)\\cdot (3\\,i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\cdot 3+{e}^{5t-3}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3(t-1)^{2}-2{e}^{5t-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3(t-1)^{2}-2{e}^{5t-3}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429198 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429198 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then accoun